But it's when you suppress it that it starts

808
00:29:56.210 --> 00:29:58.800
to crop up again and you become passive aggressive

809
00:29:58.800 --> 00:30:00.980
and then you become aggressive, aggressive.

810
00:30:00.980 --> 00:30:01.813
And

811
00:30:02.650 --> 00:30:04.510
I think that we need to feel those feelings.

812
00:30:04.510 --> 00:30:06.210
And there's decisions that you're gonna make

813
00:30:06.210 --> 00:30:09.630
in life that are not rational and that's okay, right.

814
00:30:09.630 --> 00:30:10.710
They don't have to be rational.

815
00:30:10.710 --> 00:30:12.560
I think what you wanna do is just be aware

816
00:30:12.560 --> 00:30:14.790
that you're conscious of the fact

817
00:30:14.790 --> 00:30:16.320
that you're not making a rational decision

818
00:30:16.320 --> 00:30:19.140
or you're okay sort of throwing the rational side

819
00:30:19.140 --> 00:30:19.973
of your brain out.

820
00:30:19.973 --> 00:30:24.417
Like quitting a great high-profile job to start a blog

821
00:30:24.417 --> 00:30:28.860
is not necessarily the most rational decision you can make.

822
00:30:28.860 --> 00:30:29.693
Who you marry,

823
00:30:29.693 --> 00:30:30.910
who you're in relationship with,

824
00:30:30.910 --> 00:30:32.848
what that connection is like,

825
00:30:32.848 --> 00:30:36.000
those are not purely rational decisions.

826
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:39.940
Those are very emotionally-driven chemistry,

827
00:30:39.940 --> 00:30:42.550
physiological response-based decisions.

828
00:30:42.550 --> 00:30:44.780
And I think that those are equally powerful,

829
00:30:44.780 --> 00:30:47.010
if not in some cases more powerful

830
00:30:47.010 --> 00:30:48.770
than rational decision-making.

831
00:30:48.770 --> 00:30:51.780
Yeah, I think they can be channeled to great effect

832
00:30:51.780 --> 00:30:55.850
as long as you have a healthy understanding

833
00:30:55.850 --> 00:30:57.440
of that emotional landscape.

834
00:30:57.440 --> 00:31:00.780
Like, when am I feeling a spark of inspiration

835
00:31:00.780 --> 00:31:04.900
or when am I experiencing some kind of overwhelming emotion

836
00:31:04.900 --> 00:31:09.820
that I know is driving me towards making a certain type

837
00:31:09.820 --> 00:31:11.480
of decision versus,

838
00:31:11.480 --> 00:31:13.700
oh, I'm just repeating a pattern as a result

839
00:31:13.700 --> 00:31:15.233
of my childhood trauma.

840
00:31:16.820 --> 00:31:18.500
This is gonna take me down the wrong path.

841
00:31:18.500 --> 00:31:20.930
Even though I feel strongly about doing this,

842
00:31:20.930 --> 00:31:22.590
I know well enough to know that

843
00:31:22.590 --> 00:31:24.050
that's not the right thing to do.

844
00:31:24.050 --> 00:31:26.737
But so often that becomes an excuse today too, right.

845
00:31:26.737 --> 00:31:28.010
We sort of, like,

846
00:31:28.010 --> 00:31:30.030
oh, I was brought up that way.

847
00:31:30.030 --> 00:31:31.680
But going back to what I said.
This is what I do.

848
00:31:31.680 --> 00:31:32.670
This is what I do, right.

849
00:31:32.670 --> 00:31:35.360
So we tell ourselves that narrative

850
00:31:35.360 --> 00:31:36.860
and that narrative becomes reality

851
00:31:36.860 --> 00:31:39.820
when another narrative you can replace that with.

852
00:31:39.820 --> 00:31:42.450
And often we have to replace narratives to get sort

853
00:31:42.450 --> 00:31:46.200
of better narratives is that I'm in control of my life

854
00:31:46.200 --> 00:31:48.020
and no matter what's happened to me,

855
00:31:48.020 --> 00:31:50.750
it might not be my fault that I'm in this situation

856
00:31:50.750 --> 00:31:51.910
but it's my responsibility

857
00:31:51.910 --> 00:31:53.960
how I handle this situation going forward.

858
00:31:53.960 --> 00:31:56.780
It's my responsibility to respond to the situation

859
00:31:56.780 --> 00:31:58.290
in the best way that I can.

860
00:31:58.290 --> 00:32:00.630
And I own that and nobody else owns that for me

861
00:32:00.630 --> 00:32:02.440
and I can't blame my past.

862
00:32:02.440 --> 00:32:04.240
But everything in my past has got me here

863
00:32:04.240 --> 00:32:05.073
and that's okay.

864
00:32:05.073 --> 00:32:07.300
The past has put you on this trajectory.

865
00:32:07.300 --> 00:32:09.310
It's put you at this moment in time.

866
00:32:09.310 --> 00:32:11.257
Where you go from here is completely up to you though

867
00:32:11.257 --> 00:32:13.841
and you control that and nobody else controls that.

868
00:32:13.841 --> 00:32:15.453
Boom, powerfully said.

869
00:32:16.553 --> 00:32:20.150
(dramatic swooshing)

870
00:32:20.150 --> 00:32:23.910
In the fairness versus inclusion conversation,

871
00:32:23.910 --> 00:32:26.555
it's not a matter of tipping the scales

872
00:32:26.555 --> 00:32:28.680
towards inclusion over fairness.

873
00:32:28.680 --> 00:32:31.660 line:15%
You're thinking that these things can co-exist

874
00:32:31.660 --> 00:32:33.230 line:15%
and that it's not problematic?

875
00:32:33.230 --> 00:32:35.790 line:15%
Absolutely, and I think transgender women

876
00:32:35.790 --> 00:32:37.720 line:15%
and girls have been competing with women

877
00:32:37.720 --> 00:32:40.080
and girls for years without problem,

878
00:32:40.080 --> 00:32:41.016
with their peers.

879
00:32:41.016 --> 00:32:45.070
And they've been participating on sports teams

880
00:32:45.070 --> 00:32:46.860
at the high school level,

881
00:32:46.860 --> 00:32:50.600
at the elite level and there has been no problems, right.

882
00:32:50.600 --> 00:32:52.570
And I think that what

883
00:32:53.740 --> 00:32:55.800
the discrimination against transgender women

884
00:32:55.800 --> 00:32:59.282
and girls actually does is takes away from the real issue

885
00:32:59.282 --> 00:33:03.850
about the disparity in sport and the gender inequity

886
00:33:03.850 --> 00:33:05.510
that exists in sport.

887
00:33:05.510 --> 00:33:10.033
What we really should be focusing on is women's sports

888
00:33:10.033 --> 00:33:13.430
and how we uplift women's sports.

889
00:33:13.430 --> 00:33:15.873
And I think that targeting transgender women

890
00:33:15.873 --> 00:33:17.490
does not do that.

891
00:33:17.490 --> 00:33:18.830
It doesn't help.

892
00:33:18.830 --> 00:33:22.240
The real problem is the lack of access,

893
00:33:22.240 --> 00:33:23.820
the lack of resources,

894
00:33:23.820 --> 00:33:26.860
the pay inequity that exists within women sports

895
00:33:26.860 --> 00:33:29.020
because of systemic discrimination.

896
00:33:29.020 --> 00:33:31.361
Yeah, well certainly that's for real.

897
00:33:31.361 --> 00:33:33.750
I've just put up a couple podcasts that kind

898
00:33:33.750 --> 00:33:35.040
of go pretty deep into that.

899
00:33:35.040 --> 00:33:36.543
I mean, that's a huge problem.

900
00:33:38.720 --> 00:33:40.110
In the track and field context,

901
00:33:40.110 --> 00:33:44.522
are there transgender women who are killing it?

902
00:33:44.522 --> 00:33:45.630
No.

903
00:33:45.630 --> 00:33:46.463
Their aren't?

904
00:33:46.463 --> 00:33:48.132
Tell me what (indistinct) means?

