965
00:36:18.740 --> 00:36:20.790
And what's the vision that you hold,

966
00:36:20.790 --> 00:36:22.710
like four years,

967
00:36:22.710 --> 00:36:23.796
10 years from now,

968
00:36:23.796 --> 00:36:28.140
where would you like to see the state of culture and sport?

969
00:36:28.140 --> 00:36:29.610
And we can kind of wrap it up with that,

970
00:36:29.610 --> 00:36:30.502
I think, right?

971
00:36:30.502 --> 00:36:31.580
Yeah.

972
00:36:31.580 --> 00:36:35.413
Where is this going if it was up to you?

973
00:36:35.413 --> 00:36:40.060
I think that sport is one of the most magical places

974
00:36:40.060 --> 00:36:41.620
for people to exist.

975
00:36:41.620 --> 00:36:44.440
I think that sport is a vehicle for social change

976
00:36:44.440 --> 00:36:46.740
and the change that happens within sports

977
00:36:46.740 --> 00:36:48.440
in terms of policies and acceptance

978
00:36:48.440 --> 00:36:51.540
and inclusion can really be a guide

979
00:36:51.540 --> 00:36:53.033
for the rest of the world.

980
00:36:53.033 --> 00:36:54.530
And we've seen it in the past.

981
00:36:54.530 --> 00:36:58.860
And I think that we're at a crossroads right now

982
00:36:58.860 --> 00:37:02.380
where how we treat inclusion in sport is going

983
00:37:02.380 --> 00:37:04.270
to reflect in the rest of society.

984
00:37:04.270 --> 00:37:05.103
Yeah, absolutely.

985
00:37:05.103 --> 00:37:08.930
I mean, I think I read somewhere that you were inspired

986
00:37:08.930 --> 00:37:13.240
by some of the great activist athletes out there.

987
00:37:13.240 --> 00:37:14.770
I don't know who in particular,

988
00:37:14.770 --> 00:37:17.890
but there's these iconic images that come to mind

989
00:37:17.890 --> 00:37:20.890
from Muhammad Ali to

990
00:37:21.780 --> 00:37:26.780
the closed, gloved fist on the podium at the Olympics

991
00:37:27.190 --> 00:37:32.190
and the ability of the athlete to move culture forward

992
00:37:32.750 --> 00:37:35.780
and advance conversation around ideas

993
00:37:35.780 --> 00:37:39.690
that people are resistant to is a thing.

994
00:37:39.690 --> 00:37:42.930
And I think that you're somebody who is on

995
00:37:42.930 --> 00:37:47.150
the sort of razor's edge of this

996
00:37:47.150 --> 00:37:48.770
in a new and broader

997
00:37:50.320 --> 00:37:51.875
conversation around civil rights

998
00:37:51.875 --> 00:37:54.440
and what that means and what kind of culture

999
00:37:54.440 --> 00:37:58.100
and society do we wanna be in and live in.

1000
00:37:58.100 --> 00:38:02.050
And I think your advocacy is admirable

1001
00:38:02.050 --> 00:38:05.730
and I'm in awe of your athletic talent

1002
00:38:05.730 --> 00:38:08.080
and also your strength and your courage

1003
00:38:08.080 --> 00:38:09.490
to put yourself out there

1004
00:38:11.510 --> 00:38:13.570
in harm's way, I think,

1005
00:38:13.570 --> 00:38:14.880
